    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>Normalized Ancestry Feat.</strong> Formerly granted automatically by <em>Circuitborn (Parallax Line)</em> at level 17; now available as an optional ancestry feat.</p><p><em>“Everyone is looking at the wrong thing. On purpose.”</em></p>\n        <p><strong>Perfect Misdirection (1/a Soma Break).</strong> For 1 minute, hostile creatures have roll 3d10 keep lowest 2 on attacks against you unless they succeed a Soul save at the start of their turn (DC = 8 + tier [TODO(pb-call)] + Dex) [TODO(adv-call)]. Also, once per minute you may force a ranged attack to miss by “editing the frame.”</p>",
